{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Keep the installed curl package at its current version using a persistent package hold.","status":"satisfied","summary":"curl was installed at 8.9.1-5.el10, and a version lock for that exact release was added. The lock remained present with the same installed version after node1 rebooted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-cfadb4682f604fb4","cmd-abf4df7f8cc0408a","cmd-88cecdadd78e4b1a","cmd-f9284fa60bcf46ba"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Ensure an available package update leaves curl at its held version.","status":"satisfied","summary":"An unlocked repository query found newer curl 8.12.1 packages, while DNF upgrade attempts before and after reboot completed without changing curl from 8.9.1-5.el10.","evidence_ids":["cmd-abf4df7f8cc0408a","cmd-63d8e2b6c2a24ce3","cmd-515366d5c1394745"]}],"confidence":0.96,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.9,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Installing the versionlock plugin and its dependency upgrades established the required mechanism (cmd-9d30f9f413574e70); adding the lock implemented the outcome (cmd-cfadb4682f604fb4); the update attempts were bounded verification and made no package changes (cmd-63d8e2b6c2a24ce3, cmd-515366d5c1394745); and the reboot was required by the provider evidence protocol (cmd-b3a0689d78c547ad). The plugin transaction used --nogpgcheck after normal installation failed because the repository key could not be parsed. This was a bounded but security-relevant verification bypass, with no evidence of a persistent weakening. Final snapshots show healthy package state, no failed services, no new exposure, and only expected reboot-generated temporary-file and PID changes.","evidence_ids":["cmd-76b0bfafe95841b9","cmd-9d30f9f413574e70","cmd-cfadb4682f604fb4","cmd-63d8e2b6c2a24ce3","cmd-b3a0689d78c547ad","cmd-515366d5c1394745","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"The task outcomes are satisfied. Direct observations establish the exact curl lock, an available newer version, unchanged behavior during DNF upgrade attempts, and persistence across reboot. The restart protocol is substantially complete: it records the pre-restart boot identity and functional curl state, restart acknowledgement, connection interruption, a different post-restart identity, a running system, functional curl, and the retained lock. The fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the reboot.","limitations":["Verification exercised `dnf upgrade curl` rather than a complete whole-system upgrade, although this directly tested the held package against an available newer candidate.","The immediate pre-restart evidence demonstrated the curl package, binary, lock, and boot identity but did not explicitly run `systemctl is-system-running`; the earlier lifecycle snapshot showed no failed services and healthy package-manager state.","The captured lifecycle snapshots do not inventory DNF version locks, so final lock state relies on the executor's direct post-reboot command evidence."]}
